# play/retro-achievements.md: RETROACHIEVEMENTS SETTINGS and its OFFLINE
# ACHIEVEMENTS (BETA) page. GAME SETTINGS is eleven presses up from the MAIN
# MENU's top row; on it: UPDATE GAMELISTS, MOONLIGHT GAME STREAMING, then the
# ACCOUNTS heading, then RETROACHIEVEMENTS SETTINGS -- two presses down, not
# three (two exploratory walks counted the heading, 2026-09-29). On the
# settings page: RETROACHIEVEMENTS, USERNAME, PASSWORD, WEB API KEY (fork
# builds), then OPTIONS: HARDCORE MODE, OFFLINE ACHIEVEMENTS (BETA) -- five
# presses down. The settings frame shows the account's name on its USERNAME
# row: tools/png-blackout before it is filed.
# The MAIN MENU is reached from its bottom, so the walk is the same whether
# the guest is signed in to RetroAchievements (the menu then opens on that
# row, above GAME SETTINGS) or not: up from the top row lands on BACK, the
# next on QUIT, and the rows above QUIT never move. (Until EmulationStation
# f1ae6bc25 the first press landed on an empty tab strip, #325, and every
# count here was one higher.)
key ret
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
key up
wait-for-change 30 1
key up
wait-for-change 30 1
key up
wait-for-change 30 1
key up
wait-for-change 30 1
